<title>COLOMBIA: Colombia's Carulla H1 profit up 40.5 pct.</title>
<headline>Colombia's Carulla H1 profit up 40.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Colombia's Carulla SA on Tuesday said first-half net profit jumped 40.5 percent to 3.85 billion pesos, compared with the same period last year.</p>
<p>Carulla, one of Colombia's five largest supermarket chains, reported net profits of 2.7 billion pesos for the first half of 1996.  </p>
<p>Carulla's operating income grew 26.2 percent to 185.5 billion pesos in the first half while operational expenditure increased 20.8 percent to 43.5 billion pesos, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>The results are subject to approval by Colombia's Securities Superintendency.</p>
<p>((--Javier Mozzo, Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944))</p>
